{
  "summary": "This experiment changed only the fusion strategy from concat to weighted in the multimodal setting (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool, ResNet50), achieving a validation accuracy of 0.678 and F1 of 0.646, a ~4.6-point improvement over the identical pipeline with concat fusion (0.632 acc / 0.607 F1) and ~2.8 points above the RNA-only best (0.650 acc / 0.628 F1). Because the single-variable change isolates the fusion axis, the gain is attributable to weighted fusion, indicating that ResNet50 image features carry complementary predictive signal that simple concatenation was suppressing and that proper modality weighting is necessary to unlock it. This resolves the key uncertainty from the prior concat experiment: the image modality is worth pursuing, justifying further investment in stronger image encoders (e.g., ViT-L) and alternative fusion strategies. It remains uncertain whether the weighted-fusion advantage generalizes to other image encoders, whether additional headroom exists above 0.678, and whether more sophisticated fusion mechanisms (e.g., attention-based) could yield further gains."
}

